    seeing:
      "South of Issyk-Kul, behind the Terskey Ala-Too, lies a flat upland at 3,500–4,000 m known locally as the syrt (\"raised upland\"). It is cold, open and almost treeless, with gently undulating ground dotted with lakes and marshes — a distinctive kind of high plateau landscape within the Tian Shan.",
